message: "If you use this paper, its code or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "Phenotypic insufficiency of local protein representations: fibre-preserving rearrangements of human C2H2 zinc-finger arrays reorder DNA-recognition residues under an invariant 25-spectrum"
abstract: >-
  For the 17 reviewed human C2H2 zinc-finger proteins with a non-trivial 25-fibre, 1,178
  distinct fibre-mates were drawn as random Eulerian trails. In all of them the multiset of
  fingers and the output of a window-25 local encoder are unchanged; 883 place different
  DNA-recognition residues (helix positions -1, 2, 3, 6) at some array position.
